Angular Directives:
 
What is a Directive ?
A set of classes , used for adding  some additional behaviour to the element or the component of the Angular Application.

There are three main types of directives:
They are:

1. Structural Directive:
    These are responsible for shaping and reshaping the size of DOM, handling tasks like adding, removing and manipulating the elements. 
    example: *ngFor *ngIf  *ngSwitch (most commonly used)

2. Attribute Directives:
    These are responsible for changing the appearance of html elements
    example:  (ngClass, ngModel, ngStyle)

3.  component Directives:
 responsible for controlling the rendering of the Angular components in the Angular Applications

There is one more type of directive i.e custom directive which is created by the user for defining a new behaviour.

Note: When using these structual directives we need to import common Module or classes of ngIf, ngFor,ngSwitch

*ngIf directive:
  {condinally render the html elements just like if else condition}
Benefit -> It not hide the element but compltely removes from the DOM(Document Object Model).

*ngFor directive:
  { looping over an array}
  using index,   (it is ineffiecient)
        trackBy (for effiecient appraoch )

